    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11320" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corruptrix</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conr-</span></b> ), īcis, f.
		corruptor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>she that corrupts</i> or <i>seduces;</i> or <i>adj., corrupting</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tam depravatis moribus, tam corruptrice
					provinciā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Q. Fr. 1, 1, 6, § 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">licentia, rerum corruptrix et morum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 25, 3, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
